Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 01:26:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 038/106] pinctrl: qcom: sm7150-lpass-lpi: fix swr_tx_data mux
 on gpio1

GPIO1 carries data lane 0 of the TX SoundWire bus, which is where the
WCD9375's Tx SoundWire slave lives. The pin table selects swr_tx_data
via FUNC_SEL 1 on this pin, but the silicon exposes swr_tx_data there at
FUNC_SEL 3.

With the wrong function selected the bus clock (gpio0, FUNC_SEL 2, which
is correct) is driven normally and the controller looks perfectly
healthy - frame gen comes up, SWRM_COMP_PARAMS and the frame shape read
back fine - but the codec's data line is not routed to the controller.
The Tx slave can therefore never announce itself: SWRM_MCP_SLV_STATUS
stays 0, no NEW_SLAVE_ATTACHED interrupt ever arrives, and since the
WCD9375 exposes its control regmap on the Tx link, the whole codec then
fails to probe:

  wcd937x_codec audio-codec: soundwire device init timeout
  wcd937x_codec audio-codec: ASoC error (-110): at snd_soc_component_probe()

The Rx bus was unaffected because its clk (gpio3) and data lane 0
(gpio4) are both at FUNC_SEL 2, which the table already had right.

The downstream sm6150/sdmmagpie LPI pin config (sdmmagpie = SM7150)
places tx_swr_data1 on LPI gpio19 with "func3". The mainline lpass_tlmm
node starts 18 pins into the LPI range (0x62b52000 vs the 0x62b40000 SSC
base, 18 * 0x1000), so downstream gpio19 is this driver's gpio1, and
func3 is FUNC_SEL 3. The same offset maps the WCD reset (downstream
gpio24, func2) onto this table's gpio6/cdc_pdm_rx, which confirms the
alignment.

With this, the Tx slave enumerates, the bus clash bits in SWRM_COMP_STATUS
disappear, and the codec probes and registers its capture DAIs.

Signed-off-by: Edi <woodyst@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
index 94b9b8725..e6d025e17 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm7150-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -81,7 +81,7 @@ static const char * const swr_tx_data_groups[] = { "gpio1", "gpio2", "gpio5" };
 
 static const struct lpi_pingroup sm7150_groups[] = {
 	LPI_PINGROUP(0, 0, slimbus_clk, swr_tx_clk, _, _),
-	LPI_PINGROUP(1, 2, swr_tx_data, audio_ref, _, _),
+	LPI_PINGROUP(1, 2, _, audio_ref, swr_tx_data, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(2, 4, slimbus_data, swr_tx_data, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(3, 8, slimbus_data, swr_rx_clk, _, _),
 	LPI_PINGROUP(4, 10, slimbus_data, swr_rx_data, prim_mclk_a, _),
